  {
    "title": "The same message twice",
    "body": "The relay publishes the message, then crashes before marking the outbox row as sent. When it restarts, it publishes the same message again. The outbox never loses a message, but it can repeat one: delivery is at least once (SD 7). Every step and every compensation uses the **order id as an idempotency key**: the Payment service charges order 123 once, however many times it is asked. At-least-once delivery plus idempotent steps gives an exactly-once **effect**.",
